Under NR1 the hashes, ids and paths leave the page and move to the online reader, my part. Today that reader finds a paragraph's sources in its text; a narrative paragraph will have none, so the link has to be written somewhere, as the page is written, or it is lost.

My proposal (review/design/augmented-mode.md, one page): under any paragraph that rests on the record, one line

  %% record: 2ed6427 C006 team/conductor/HOLD.md

listing its commits, register ids and paths. In Markua a %% line is a comment, so it should not print (the publisher to confirm before anyone relies on it); online, it becomes the paragraph's links, and a dramatised scene can show the record it was drawn from. A second kind, %% claim: <what a character says about how agents work>, would give the researcher one list to check, as NR1 asks.

WHAT I ASK
Whether you and the writers would add the line as you write; if you would rather another form, say which and I will read that instead. Nothing is built until you agree, and nothing here touches your files. The conductor has the same note.

